<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Suren</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Suren-Pahlav</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Suren was one of the great noble families of Parthian and Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, with its estates in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sakastan</a>, the present-day Sistan. Under the Arsacids its head held the hereditary right to crown the king, and its most famous member, the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surena">Surena</a>, destroyed the Roman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carrhae">Carrhae</a> in 53 BCE. The family remained powerful under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a>.</p></div>
